From: Liuqin Linux Kit <liuqin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: synchronize DPCM audio with link teardown and restore

The Qualcomm downstream driver stops its audio backend before disabling
the stream. Mainline waits for userspace PCM closure after PUSH_IDLE.
A jack notification does not acknowledge DSP teardown, and restoring only
SDP/ACR after resetting the link leaves AudioReach DMA stalled.

Add a synchronous HDMI-codec link notification, separate from jack state.
DPCM excludes playback backends with an unavailable codec link, closes
them before returning, then reapplies parameters and restarts backends
for still-open frontends when the link is ready. Serialize availability
and route changes with the card PCM mutex. Forward runtime-update errors
instead of losing backend start/stop failures. Legacy callers and static
PCM links keep their existing behavior; capture paths are unaffected.

MSM DP sends this notification before PUSH_IDLE or PHY teardown and after
DPU confirms the first frame, not inside the pre-kickoff bridge enable.
Cancel pending restoration on teardown. For link-managed playback, defer
HDMI engine shutdown until component close, after CPU DAI shutdown has
stopped the DSP graph. Leave DSP commands out of PCM trigger to avoid
blocking period callbacks sharing the response worker. Legacy and capture
shutdown timing is unchanged. Serialize the remaining ALSA/MMIO state with an
audio mutex, cache deferred preparation and cancel it on shutdown. Retain
physical jack notifications without synthesizing unplug during modesets,
and remove the userspace-close completion timeout.

Reference: LineageOS/android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8450-modules
3b30ba7df6608c97c0ba2d55d679a6b5987c4c66, msm/dp/dp_audio.c, dp_display.c,
and audio-kernel/asoc/codecs/msm_hdmi_codec_rx.c. This is a Qualcomm
downstream reference, not proof of shipping M81 source identity.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_audio_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_audio_helper.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_audio_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_audio_helper.c
@@ -127,6 +127,55 @@
 	mutex_unlock(&connector->hdmi_audio.lock);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(drm_connector_hdmi_audio_plugged_notify);
+
+static int drm_connector_hdmi_audio_hook_link_cb(struct device *dev, void *data,
+						hdmi_codec_link_cb fn,
+						struct device *codec_dev)
+{
+	struct drm_connector *connector = data;
+	int ret = 0;
+
+	guard(mutex)(&connector->hdmi_audio.lock);
+	if (fn)
+		ret = fn(codec_dev, connector->hdmi_audio.last_link_state);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	connector->hdmi_audio.link_cb = fn;
+	connector->hdmi_audio.link_cb_dev = codec_dev;
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/**
+ * drm_connector_hdmi_audio_link_notify - synchronize an audio link reset
+ * @connector: connector whose stream is being stopped or restored
+ * @active: false before link teardown, true after successful stream enable
+ *
+ * DPCM backends are stopped synchronously before returning from a false
+ * notification, and reopened with their existing frontend parameters on true.
+ * This does not change jack status. The caller must not hold locks acquired
+ * by its audio prepare/shutdown callbacks. Drivers that do not call this
+ * function retain their existing backend lifecycle.
+ *
+ * Return: 0 on success or a negative backend error.
+ */
+int drm_connector_hdmi_audio_link_notify(struct drm_connector *connector,
+					bool active)
+{
+	int ret = 0;
+
+	guard(mutex)(&connector->hdmi_audio.lock);
+	if (connector->hdmi_audio.last_link_state == active)
+		return 0;
+
+	if (connector->hdmi_audio.link_cb)
+		ret = connector->hdmi_audio.link_cb(connector->hdmi_audio.link_cb_dev,
+						    active);
+	if (!ret)
+		connector->hdmi_audio.last_link_state = active;
+	return ret;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(drm_connector_hdmi_audio_link_notify);
 
 static const struct hdmi_codec_ops drm_connector_hdmi_audio_ops = {
 	.audio_startup = drm_connector_hdmi_audio_startup,
